New Feature 1: Debt Restructuring & Asset Liquidation Exchange (Custom Queue-Based Emergency Fund)
How it works: Since players cannot sell houses or mortgage properties, when a player is on the brink of debt, this feature allows them to put an owned property up for emergency auction to the other active players in queue order.

DSA Used: Uses your custom LinkedQueue to iterate through active players, offering them the property for a discounted cash injection to keep the debtor in the game.

Why it's advanced: It dynamically trades ownership pointers (PropertySquare.owner) mid-turn using only pure queue traversal without breaking the turn order or violating base Monopoly constraints.

Code for Replacement Feature 1 (Player.java):
Java
public boolean emergencyAssetAuction(PropertySquare prop, LinkedQueue<Player> activeQueue, int debtAmount) {
    System.out.println("--- EMERGENCY ASSET AUCTION ---");
    System.out.println(this.name + " is offering " + prop.getName() + " to active players for $" + debtAmount);
    
    int size = activeQueue.size();
    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
        Player buyer = activeQueue.dequeue();
        activeQueue.enqueue(buyer); // Keep queue order unchanged
        
        if (!buyer.equals(this) && buyer.cash >= debtAmount) {
            // Transfer cash and ownership
            buyer.cash -= debtAmount;
            this.cash += debtAmount;
            this.owned.remove(prop);
            buyer.owned.add(prop);
            prop.setOwner(buyer);
            
            System.out.println("AUCTION SUCCESS: " + buyer.name + " purchased " + prop.getName() + "!");
            return true;
        }
    }
    System.out.println("AUCTION FAILED: No player could afford the asset.");
    return false;
}
